[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":81},["ShallowReactive",2],{"work-\u002Fworks\u002Fdeep-empty-wide-open":3},{"id":4,"title":5,"body":6,"collaborators":67,"description":68,"extension":69,"img":70,"meta":71,"navigation":47,"path":72,"roles":67,"seo":73,"stem":74,"tags":75,"type":78,"url":67,"year":79,"__hash__":80},"works\u002Fworks\u002Fdeep-empty-wide-open.md","Deep Empty - Wide Open",{"type":7,"value":8,"toc":63},"minimark",[9,13,30,33,48],[10,11,12],"p",{},"Collaboration with Valerie Messini.",[10,14,15,16,23,24,29],{},"The installation is based on an idea by Valerie Messini which is outlined ",[17,18,22],"a",{"href":19,"rel":20},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.researchcatalogue.net\u002Fview\u002F1942520\u002F1942434?c=0",[21],"nofollow","here",". In short, we use Generative Adversarial Networks (i.e., an architecture called ",[17,25,28],{"href":26,"rel":27},"https:\u002F\u002Fjunyanz.github.io\u002FCycleGAN\u002F",[21],"CycleGAN",") to learn a mapping from pictures of humans to pictures of sea horizons in a semi-supervised way. In the live installation, live videos of visitors are then transformed into sea horizon images.",[10,31,32],{},"The resulting images\u002Fvideos are somewhat reminiscent of impressionist paintings, and the installation invites visitors to interactively explore the generative capabilities of the algorithm with facial expressions and gestures.",[34,35,38],"div",{"className":36},[37],"video-container",[39,40],"iframe",{"className":41,"src":43,"title":44,"frameBorder":45,"allow":46,"allowFullScreen":47},[42],"video","https:\u002F\u002Fwww.youtube.com\u002Fembed\u002FsANmhNoloiI?si=ft4-K50rsF2Jaz6j","YouTube video player","0","accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share",true,[10,49,50,51,56,57,62],{},"Exhibited at ",[17,52,55],{"href":53,"rel":54},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.artemis-gallery.net\u002F",[21],"Artemis Gallery Lisbon"," in the exhibition ",[17,58,61],{"href":59,"rel":60},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.